<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-380-2026-11-29 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-380 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 9.63 s, kick 3.459 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 16868 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.5410-0.001321*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
ILLUSTRATIVE. PRE-FLIGHT. USSF-380, Falcon 9, SLC-4E. T0 is the window open 2026-11-29T04:39:00Z (Sat 28 Nov 8:39 p.m. PT). SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf380 header: 28 Nov 23:39 ET to 29 Nov 03:39 ET, a four-hour window to 08:39Z. Backup Sun 29 Nov 6:26 p.m. PT = 2026-11-30T02:26:00Z. 27th flight of the first stage. Landing on Of Course I Still Love You. LL2 id b0d27def-0a88-44c3-a947-1fd5b8503e2c status Go at 04:39Z, window 04:39-08:39Z, last_updated 2026-11-26T11:45:38Z.
Published timeline (SpaceX ussf380): Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:57, entry burn 6:04-6:27, landing burn 8:02, landing 8:25. SECO, orbit and deploy are not published. Payload is classified. No unofficial satellite count is used. SpaceX does not name the booster.
INFERRED/ASSUMED: SECO-1 at T+519 s and a 177.3 x 266.2 km parking orbit are borrowed from the Group 15 / USSF-317 config, not from USSF-380. LL2&#x27;s mission text says the drop zones match previous Starlink Group 15 launches. File ends 2 revs after cutoff (deploy unpublished). Booster entry and landing are not modelled.
Target (see launch config): insertion 177 km, apoapsis 266 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 153.18 deg; payload 16868 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-29T04:39:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (SpaceX publishes no SECO, restart or deploy time for USSF-380 (classified payload). Propagated 2 revs on the inferred insertion orbit. The insertion altitude is borrowed, not a USSF-380 element.). From insertion T+519.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 88.93 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11191 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 177.21 km, osculating 174.5 x 268.8 km, i 68.016 deg.</description>
